- **Unit:** blitz-tests
  - **Path:** tests/blitz-tests
  - **What it is:** Integration tests (tests/blitz-tests/lib.rs:1) covering accessibility (tests/blitz-tests/tests/accessibility_hidden.rs:14; tests/blitz-tests/tests/accessibility_roles.rs:1-7) and, since 2026-10-10-snapshot-states, the builder's three state attributes on a parsed page — every value of each grammar, on a role that supports the attribute and one that does not, `aria-checked` read on a checkable role alone and neither attribute on a native checkbox or radio, a 5,500-character `aria-checked` nowhere in the tree, 5 tests in both layout modes, run by the workspace test leg and per package and not by the `a11y` CI leg, which runs six named files since 2026-10-14-stand-a11y-assertions, this one not among them (tests/blitz-tests/tests/accessibility_states.rs:134-316); the builder's merged `aria-expanded` · `aria-disabled` · `aria-level` reads, 3 tests (tests/blitz-tests/tests/accessibility_merged_states.rs:88-157), the unread `aria-activedescendant` pinned, 1 test (tests/blitz-tests/tests/accessibility_active_descendant_unread.rs:39-81), and an `inert` subtree skipped by Tab and Shift+Tab, passed through by a hit, absent from the tree and restored when `inert` is removed, the focus-fixup limit pinned, 4 tests (tests/blitz-tests/tests/inert_subtree.rs:68-194), each in both layout modes; block, inline, flex, grid, abspos/fixed and `display: contents` layout (tests/blitz-tests/tests/comment_layout.rs:1-7; tests/blitz-tests/tests/display_contents.rs:1-2; tests/blitz-tests/tests/flex_grid_order.rs:1-4; tests/blitz-tests/tests/oof_dynamic_cb.rs:1-5); inline text layout (tests/blitz-tests/tests/whitespace_modes.rs:15-25; tests/blitz-tests/tests/line_break.rs:1-2; tests/blitz-tests/tests/inline_box_baseline.rs:1-2; tests/blitz-tests/tests/br_trailing_line.rs:1-2; tests/blitz-tests/tests/inline_fragment_rects.rs:1-4);
 painting (tests/blitz-tests/tests/background_size.rs:1; tests/blitz-tests/tests/svg_background_size.rs:1; tests/blitz-tests/tests/outset_box_shadow_shape.rs:1-4; tests/blitz-tests/tests/paint_order.rs:1-2; tests/blitz-tests/tests/scrollbars.rs:1-4); paint tree and hit testing, a hit past a node dropped since the last resolve included (tests/blitz-tests/tests/paint_tree_incremental.rs:1-4; tests/blitz-tests/tests/pointer_events.rs:1-4; tests/blitz-tests/tests/hit_test_dropped_nodes.rs:32-82); input (tests/blitz-tests/tests/touch_events.rs:1-4; tests/blitz-tests/tests/touch_action.rs:1-3; tests/blitz-tests/tests/scrollbar_drag.rs:1; tests/blitz-tests/tests/text_selection_anonymous_block.rs:1-8; tests/blitz-tests/tests/details_element.rs:1-3); scrolling and fragment navigation (tests/blitz-tests/tests/fragment_navigation.rs:1-2), and an into-view scroll through nested scrolling boxes with the visible-region reader — 7 tests, in both layout modes (tests/blitz-tests/tests/scroll_into_view_nested.rs:1-10); a range input's default actions, since 2026-10-13-range-input-interaction — `range_input_interaction`, 8 tests on parsed pages (6 until 2026-10-14-stand-requirement-sweep), each in both layout modes: the arrows, Home and End stepping a focused range input with one `input` per change, a click setting the value by position and focusing it, degenerate attributes keeping the value finite, bounded and on its grid, a decimal step reading its decimals, a disabled range input taking neither keys nor a click, and attribute writes re-seeding and re-sanitizing the value (tests/blitz-tests/tests/range_input_interaction.rs:117-302) and, since 2026-10-14-stand-requirement-sweep, removing `value` re-seeding it, removing `step`, `min` or `max` re-sanitizing it, and a `type` change clearing the range data and a change back re-seeding it (tests/blitz-tests/tests/range_input_interaction.rs:304-409);
 a scrolled box's own geometry and the hit at a box that clips, since 2026-10-10-scrolling-box-bounds-and-hit, each in both layout modes — `scrolled_box_client_rect`, 7 tests (a scrolled box's client rect, the nested case, the readers re-based on it and, since 2026-10-14-stand-requirement-sweep, a `writing-mode: vertical-lr` box scrolled (70, 120) reading its unscrolled rect, green under both builds), `hit_clipped_at_scrolling_box`, 13 tests (a hit stopped at the padding box of a box that clips by `overflow`, the one-axis case, a `contain: paint` box stopping the hit at its padding box and, since 2026-10-14-stand-requirement-sweep, the hits at an `img`, inside an `iframe`'s sub-document and inside a filled text `input`, and a box both transformed and scrolled hit where its rows show) and `scrolled_box_absolute_position`, 1 test (a scrolled box's `Node::absolute_position` read where it stands) (tests/blitz-tests/tests/scrolled_box_client_rect.rs:134-364; tests/blitz-tests/tests/hit_clipped_at_scrolling_box.rs:187-400; tests/blitz-tests/tests/scrolled_box_absolute_position.rs:52-82); `transformed_client_rect`, 4 tests in both layout modes — a translated box, a scaled box and a translated parent's child read where their transforms move them while the child's offset rect does not, and a target inside a translated scrolling box reading outside its visible region (tests/blitz-tests/tests/transformed_client_rect.rs:79-220); style invalidation, transforms, units, transitions (tests/blitz-tests/tests/style_property_invalidation.rs:1-2; tests/blitz-tests/tests/transform_2d_subset.rs:1-2; tests/blitz-tests/tests/rem_after_viewport_change.rs:1-2; tests/blitz-tests/tests/pseudo_element_update.rs:1-3); mutation and leaks (tests/blitz-tests/tests/anonymous_block_leak.rs:1-2; tests/blitz-tests/tests/inner_html_leak.rs:1);
 Dioxus integration (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stale_node_mapping.rs:18-23; tests/blitz-tests/tests/harness_smoke.rs:102-113); `<link>` stylesheet loading (tests/blitz-tests/tests/link_rel_attribute.rs:1-2; tests/blitz-tests/tests/render_blocking_stylesheet.rs:1-8); the seven_guis headless stand — mount, bundled-font text, fresh-boot and incremental identity, offline, one driven interaction per lean task, timer ticks, one stable element id per element (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_boot.rs:1-3; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_counter.rs:1-2; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_flight_booker.rs:1-3; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_timer.rs:1-3; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_crud.rs:1-3; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_element_ids.rs:1-5); Dioxus falsy boolean-attribute clearing — `disabled` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/dioxus_falsy_disabled.rs:1-6) and the 28 names of its own list on both attribute paths (the bridge's predicate upstream's 28-name `is_bool_attr` since 2026-10-13-upstream-sync-polish-and-ship; `inert` the 28th name the check reads since 2026-10-13-stand-keyboard-harness, the attribute half only — a truthy `inert` honoured — `inert_subtree`, `stand_keyboard` — and a falsy one cleared by the bridge), a falsy `hidden` leaving the element displayed and a snapshot node (tests/blitz-tests/tests/dioxus_falsy_boolean_attrs.rs:1-8); the snapshot's per-control state through real input, and the password mask on an in-file fixture (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_snapshot_state.rs:1-10);
 the stand checks' shared module `tests/common/mod.rs` — no test target and no test in it, the one statement of the per-task tables `controls`, `tab_order`, `INPUT_NAMES` and `rendered` — joined at 2026-10-14-stand-a11y-assertions by `ENABLED_TAB_ORDER` (the flight booker after `flight-return`, CRUD after a row is selected) and `REGION_NAMES` (`crud-list` → `People`) (tests/blitz-tests/tests/common/mod.rs:72-99; tests/blitz-tests/tests/common/mod.rs:133-136) — and of seven helpers — `tab_order` (CRUD six stops, `crud-list` third) and the helper `focused` moved in from `stand_accessibility_ids` and `stand_snapshot_state` since 2026-10-13-stand-keyboard-harness — read through `mod common;` by 21 stand checks (`stand_contrast` the eighteenth, since 2026-10-13-stand-contrast-harness, `stand_keyboard` the nineteenth, since 2026-10-13-stand-keyboard-harness, and `stand_requirement_sweep` and `stand_non_lean_tasks` the twentieth and twenty-first, since 2026-10-14-stand-requirement-sweep) (tests/blitz-tests/tests/common/mod.rs:1-6; tests/blitz-tests/tests/common/mod.rs:48-70; tests/blitz-tests/tests/common/mod.rs:101-121); since 2026-10-13-stand-keyboard-harness the stand keyboard check `stand_keyboard`, 14 tests in both layout modes (11 until 2026-10-14-stand-a11y-assertions, which added the last three and put it in the `a11y` CI leg) — Tab and Shift+Tab walking each lean task's stated sequence with wrap, the engine's focus, the snapshot's `focused` and the tree's focus agreeing at every step; Enter and Space on each focused stand button read as its click, 20 rows; the controls HTML gives the keys, a button disabled after it took focus and a button that is itself scrolled, on in-file fixtures; a click focusing each stand button; a `disabled` attribute skipping a form control by Tab and not a `<div disabled tabindex=0>`;
 the CRUD list taking focus and its keys moving the selection; the Apple delete binding on every OS; an inert subtree skipped by Tab; and, since 2026-10-14-stand-a11y-assertions, the walk beyond boot — the flight booker after `flight-return` (six stops) and CRUD after a row is selected (eight stops), each state reached by keyboard alone and walked in `ENABLED_TAB_ORDER` — every `controls(task)` id reached by Tab (an empty set difference against `tab_order` and `ENABLED_TAB_ORDER` over every lean task), and Enter and Space on the later-enabled `crud-update` and `crud-delete` each read as its click (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_keyboard.rs:248-279; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_keyboard.rs:302-333; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_keyboard.rs:335-353; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_keyboard.rs:124-152; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_keyboard.rs:154-210; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_keyboard.rs:575-602; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_keyboard.rs:614-655; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_keyboard.rs:657-717; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_keyboard.rs:752-779); the driver session over the stand — state, focus and timer time held across commands on one `Session`, ids before and after a command, a held instance reading as a fresh boot, the socket lifecycle and each of its edges with, since 2026-10-10-driver-cli, a call that runs and one that is refused over the socket, requests outside the protocol refused with nothing run, and a host with no request for its idle expiry ending as `stop` does, and nothing of the screen written by a session host that installs no log sink — it leaves that host only as the answer to a call (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_session_state.rs:1-4; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_session_ids.rs:1-5; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_session_fresh.rs:1-5; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_session_lifecycle.rs:1-7; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_session_quiet.rs:1-7);
 a recorded session — `stand_session_recording`: the four lean tasks recorded, each record ending with its kept answer (a shot's `{"width","height"}`, no `png` and no shot's first 64 base64 characters), and replayed through `Check::replay` in both layout modes — each script ending `snapshot` · `screenshot`, so the shot path's kept form is covered in process on each unix OS CI runs (linux, macOS; the file is unix only, as recording is) — a typed password kept as the stand-in, a recording directory open to its group refused with nothing written (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_session_recording.rs:108-286); the committed checks replayed — `stand_replay`, 3 tests in both layout modes, not unix-gated: each committed check holding on a fresh stand Counter, each red at its first activation step (1 for the command line's check, 3 for the MCP role's) on a test-local variant `Counter` that adds 2, every earlier step held and `changed` among its keys, and a check on a session of another app running nothing, its failure messages holding the mode, the file and a step index alone (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_replay.rs:81-110; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_replay.rs:198-234; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_replay.rs:236-258); settle on a held instance — a Timer step returning with its delayed update present and no sleep, an idle settle changing nothing, and on in-file fixtures a write made while mounting, a load in flight read as not settled until it is answered, a running animation reported and not waited on, a hover that moves with layout, and two instances that never go quiet ending at the bound, in both layout modes (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_settle.rs:1-9);
 the driver's calls run on a held stand session through `Session::run` — the twelve files `stand_act_ids`, `stand_act_diff`, `stand_act_timer`, `stand_act_refused`, `stand_act_keys`, `stand_act_range`, `stand_act_disabled`, `stand_act_obstructed`, `stand_act_scroll`, `stand_act_spans`, since 2026-10-10-driver-cli `stand_act_filled` and, since 2026-10-10-snapshot-states, `stand_act_states`, 42 tests (41 until 2026-10-14-stand-requirement-sweep added `stand_act_obstructed`'s sixth) and two ignored children: one id read by the snapshot, the accessibility tree and the driver, the diff a step returns, a step that changes a control's pressed, selected or invalid reading returning that node as it reads after the step, time moved by `advance`, a refused call changing nothing and an id told `stale` from `not-found`, focus moves and a deleting key — and, since 2026-10-13-stand-keyboard-harness, `press enter` and `press space` on a Tab-focused button each counting as its click (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_act_keys.rs:131-165) —, the range input moved by the driver's `click` and keys — since 2026-10-13-range-input-interaction, its value changes named by the diff on the slider (`value`) and on its display (`name`), where until then it pinned a measured no-op (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_act_range.rs:1-10) —, a control refused while it reads not enabled and acted on once it reads enabled, a covered and an out-of-view target refused on in-file fixtures
 — since 2026-10-14-stand-requirement-sweep also a target beside a box clipped on one axis, refused `covered` with the instance unchanged (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_act_obstructed.rs:560-605) —, an out-of-view row brought into view by `scroll` and then clicked, a `type` that leaves exactly its text in a filled control and clears it with an empty text, a masked control's written form holding the mask and never the typed text, the two engine readings fixed at 2026-10-10-scrolling-box-bounds-and-hit — a scrolled box reading the same bounds after its content is scrolled and unnamed in that scroll's diff, a `click` naming it landing on the row at its centre, and a control lying where a box's scrolled-out rows extend clicked as itself — and the one command span a call leaves, read from a sink capture in a re-run child — one `escher_driver` line per call holding its verb, a refused call's cause, an acting call's settle reading and the lengths of its diff, none at the default level, and no id, name or typed text anywhere in the capture — in both layout modes (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_act_ids.rs:1-15; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_act_diff.rs:1-13; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_act_timer.rs:1-12; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_act_refused.rs:1-9; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_act_keys.rs:1-10; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_act_range.rs:1-10; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_act_disabled.rs:1-8; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_act_obstructed.rs:1-19; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_act_scroll.rs:1-14; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_act_spans.rs:1-23; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_act_filled.rs:56-260; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_act_states.rs:79-158);
 since 2026-10-12-headless-screenshot a thirteenth driver-action file, `stand_act_screenshot` — the whole screen a PNG of the harness's raster with text painted, an element shot its bounds rounded outward, a shot refused as every id-addressed call is, an app with no usable font refused `fonts-unavailable` with nothing changed, a typed password never leaving as pixels and a shot changing nothing, in both layout modes (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_act_screenshot.rs:80-302) — and a fourteenth, `stand_act_transformed`, a `click` on a translated button accepted and landing and its snapshot `bounds` read where it shows, 2 tests in both layout modes (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_act_transformed.rs:76-116), a fifteenth, `stand_act_select`, a select driven by id — at boot its node, `ComboBox` with its name and value and its options as its children, `type` with a label choosing that option, a click then a key, the Tab walk skipping a disabled select, a disabled select and an unchosen option refused — 5 tests in both layout modes (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_act_select.rs:79-256), the engine check `select_interaction`, no `stand_*` file — the select's box, its seed, keys and typeahead over one second of the document's clock, a disabled select, a re-seed — 7 tests in both layout modes (tests/blitz-tests/tests/select_interaction.rs:113-343), `stand_screenshot_repeat` — a shot of one state byte-identical in two child runs and in the parent on one host, 12 shots in both layout modes — a shot's PNG bytes differ between linux x86_64 and macOS aarch64, so a check compared byte for byte across OSes holds no `screenshot` step (as measured at CI#39225375577) (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_screenshot_repeat.rs:75-98)
 — and the engine check `password_painted_masked` — a text input painting its characters, two password values of one length painting the same frame, a password input painting its bullets and a focused one its caret, in both layout modes (tests/blitz-tests/tests/password_painted_masked.rs:84-131); since 2026-10-13-stand-contrast-harness the stand contrast check `stand_contrast`, 5 tests in both layout modes (2 until 2026-10-14-stand-a11y-assertions) — the 18 `controls(task)` rows over the four lean tasks at boot each read through `Harness::text_contrast` against a stated record, pass 14 · fail 0 · exempt-inactive 3 · no-text 1 since the stand's accent moved one step darker at 2026-10-14-stand-a11y-assertions (pass 9 · fail 5 until then; the five former fails `counter-increment`, `flight-one-way`, `flight-book`, `timer-reset` and `crud-create` now `#ffffff` on `#3a5ce5` at 5.47), exempt exactly where the snapshot's `enabled` reads `Some(false)`, and the painted background matching the measured one within 1 per channel; since that chunk it also asserts every non-exempt control row, the CRUD list rows and the text outside the controls (`TEXT_ROWS`, 14, all pass) and the colour states it reaches, hover and active included (`STATE_ROWS`, 19: 18 pass, 1 exempt), one shared reader classifying all three tables, and runs in the `a11y` CI leg (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_contrast.rs:49-137; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_contrast.rs:481-512; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_contrast.rs:514-564; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_contrast.rs:577-605; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_contrast.rs:607-635; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_contrast.rs:637-661); since 2026-10-10-mcp-surface an MCP session driven in process
 — `serve_mcp` over in-memory streams completing the Counter flow by tool calls alone, one `tool_call` span per call the parent of each `command` span, read by a hand-written in-process recorder, in both layout modes (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_mcp_tools.rs:176-223; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_mcp_tools.rs:225-397), and since 2026-10-12-self-description every cause a tool call reaches served with its remedy, `covered` on an overlay fixture, and `help` answered by the server, parenting no `command` span (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_mcp_tools.rs:408-577; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_mcp_tools.rs:768-820); since 2026-10-12-self-description `stand_mcp_masked` — a password typed through an MCP `type` reads `MASKED_VALUE` and never the typed text, role `PasswordInput` with a non-empty name, in both layout modes; it declares no `mod session_common;` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_mcp_masked.rs:67-143); since 2026-10-14-stand-requirement-sweep, three targets, each auto-discovered with no `[[test]]` table — `stand_requirement_sweep`, 2 tests in both layout modes: every requirement held through `Session::run` alone on each lean task (the screen inside `SNAPSHOT_TEXT_BUDGET`, one distinct id per node line, each an accessibility node's `author_id`, one id-addressed acting call settled with the diff the check reads itself, an empty diff for a click on `task-title`, `press tab` focusing the first Tab stop, two byte-equal 800 × 600 shots, an unread id refused `not-found`), and `WITNESSES`, 16 rows in requirement order naming each requirement's witness tests, each found in its file through `include_str!` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_requirement_sweep.rs:85-211; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_requirement_sweep.rs:233-613); `stand_non_lean_tasks`, 3 tests in both layout modes
 — the per-task count of elements that react to a click and state no role (0 on the four lean tasks, Home and Temperature Converter, Circle Drawer 1, Cells 676, measured and pinned), the Circle Drawer dialog rule applying, and its open dialog read keyed (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_non_lean_tasks.rs:93-148); and `password_caret_click`, 2 tests in both layout modes, a password's click-placed caret on one index for two values of one length, narrow and wide, and a double click selecting the whole value (tests/blitz-tests/tests/password_caret_click.rs:83-121); and what the checks that hold a session share, the module `tests/session_common/mod.rs` — no test target and no test in it, read through `mod session_common;` by five of the session checks, by `stand_settle`, by the fifteen `stand_act_*`, since 2026-10-10-mcp-surface, by `stand_mcp_tools` and, since 2026-10-12-headless-screenshot, by `stand_screenshot_repeat` and, since 2026-10-14-stand-requirement-sweep, by `stand_requirement_sweep` and by `stand_virtual_clock`, and by `stand_replay` — the readers counted below —, and holding since 2026-10-07-act-by-id the driver's call builders, an outcome reader and a focus reader beside the session helpers, since 2026-10-07-refusal-detection the `scroll` builder and two refusal readers — the cause of a refused call, and that cause with whether the snapshot and both focus readings stayed equal —, since 2026-10-10-driver-cli the `snapshot` builder and since 2026-10-12-headless-screenshot the two `screenshot` builders and the `shot` reader, and `shot_prefix`, the first 64 base64 characters of a whole-screen shot as the driver writes it (tests/blitz-tests/tests/session_common/mod.rs:1-7; tests/blitz-tests/tests/session_common/mod.rs:271-281; tests/blitz-tests/tests/session_common/mod.rs:119-158)
